24 13194139534289 17592186045417 true] [17592186417735 1075 #edb/ref 17592186417726 13194139534289 17592186045417 true] [17592186417735 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534289 17592186045417 true] [17592186417735 1077 "selection" 13194139534289 17592186045417 true] [17592186417735 1078 #edb/ref 17592186417712 13194139534289 17592186045417 true] [17592186417735 1079 #uuid "59767641-5ff1-522d-98ff-ca8331e026ef" 13194139534289 17592186045417 true] [17592186417736 1075 #edb/ref 17592186417711 13194139534289 17592186045417 true] [17592186417736 1075 #edb/ref 17592186417718 13194139534289 17592186045417 true] [17592186417736 1075 #edb/ref 17592186417720 13194139534289 17592186045417 true] [17592186417736 1075 #edb/ref 17592186417730 13194139534289 17592186045417 true] [17592186417736 1075 #edb/ref 17592186417732 13194139534289 17592186045417 true] [17592186417736 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534289 17592186045417 true] [17592186417736 1077 "selection" 13194139534289 17592186045417 true] [17592186417736 1078 #edb/ref 17592186417711 13194139534289 17592186045417 true] [17592186417736 1079 #uuid "9debef96-eaa3-515c-b307-163bd264f5ea" 13194139534289 17592186045417 true] [17592186417737 1075 #edb/ref 17592186417709 13194139534289 17592186045417 true] [17592186417737 1075 #edb/ref 17592186417710 13194139534289 17592186045417 true] [17592186417737 1075 #edb/ref 17592186417715 13194139534289 17592186045417 true] [17592186417737 1075 #edb/ref 17592186417716 13194139534289 17592186045417 true] [17592186417737 1075 #edb/ref 17592186417727 13194139534289 17592186045417 true] [17592186417737 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534289 17592186045417 true] [17592186417737 1077 "selection" 13194139534289 17592186045417 true] [17592186417737 1078 #edb/ref 17592186417709 13194139534289 17592186045417 true] [17592186417737 1079 #uuid "e63daa46-8b3f-5be5-a899-eeb5be3faafc" 13194139534289 17592186045417 true] [17592186417738 1068 #edb/ref 17592186417733 13194139534289 17592186045417 true] [17592186417738 1069 "q-34382" 13194139534289 17592186045417 true] [17592186417738 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534289 17592186045417 true] [17592186417738 1071 "Consider the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 4 & 2 & -6\\end{aligned}]$ and the vector $b=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ k \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].$ Find the value of $k$ such that $b\\in \\text{Null}(A).$" 13194139534289 17592186045417 true] [17592186417738 1072 #uuid "3276f9dc-0fc5-5be4-8351-1b5347481225" 13194139534289 17592186045417 true] [17592186417738 1074 "If $b\\in \\text{Null}(A),$ then we must have $Ab=0.$ Substituting the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ab & =0 \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 4 & 2 & -6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ k \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}3+k+2 \\\\ 4+2k+6\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis corresponds to the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}k+5=0 \\\\ 2k+10=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand for each of these equations, we obtain $k=-5.$" 13194139534289 17592186045417 true] [17592186417739 1068 #edb/ref 17592186417737 13194139534289 17592186045417 true] [17592186417739 1069 "q-74858" 13194139534289 17592186045417 true] [17592186417739 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534289 17592186045417 true] [17592186417739 1071 "The matrix $A$ and vectors ${b}_{1}$, ${b}_{2}$, ${b}_{3}$ are given below. Which of the vectors lie in $\\text{Null}(A)?$\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" 13194139534289 17592186045417 true] [17592186417739 1072 #uuid "840cf185-0fde-50bc-83f8-78075677882d" 13194139534289 17592186045417 true] [17592186417739 1074 "A vector $b$ lies in $\\text{Null}(A)$ if $Ab=0.$ So, we need to compute the product of $A$ and each of the given vectors and check whether it is equal to $0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A{b}_{1} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\ne 0\\,\\times  \\\\ A{b}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\ne 0\\,\\times  \\\\ A{b}_{3} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]\\ne 0\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, none of the vectors lies in $\\text{Null}(A).$" 13194139534289 17592186045417 true] [17592186417740 1068 #edb/ref 17592186417735 13194139534289 17592186045417 true] [17592186417740 1069 "q-111154" 13194139534289 17592186045417 true] [17592186417740 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534289 17592186045417 true] [17592186417740 1071 "Consider the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 6 \\\\ 4 & -8\\end{aligned}].$ Find $\\text{Null}(A).$" 13194139534289 17592186045417 true] [17592186417740 1072 #uuid "87edb91a-a643-5fdb-a1df-2e5d059d6b9b" 13194139534289 17592186045417 true] [17592186417740 1074 "We need to solve the equation $Ax=0.$ First, we find the row echelon form of $A$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 6 \\\\ 4 & -8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis corresponds to the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ 0=0 \\\\ 0=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variable is ${x}_{1}$, and we have one free variable, ${x}_{2}.$ That means we need to find ${x}_{1}$ in terms of ${x}_{2}.$\n\nFrom the first equation we get ${x}_{1}=2{x}_{2},$ so the set of all the solutions of $Ax=0$ is\n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)={[\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2}\\in R}.\n$$" 13194139534289 17592186045417 true] [17592186417741 1068 #edb/ref 17592186417734 13194139534289 17592186045417 true] [17592186417741 1069 "q-111103" 13194139534289 17592186045417 true] [17592186417741 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534289 17592186045417 true] [17592186417741 1071 "Consider the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -6 \\\\ -1 & 3 \\\\ 4 & -12\\end{aligned}]$ and the vector $b=[\\begin{aligned}k \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$ Find the value of $k$ such that $b\\in \\text{Null}(A).$" 13194139534289 17592186045417 true] [17592186417741 1072 #uuid "89126de9-6477-52ae-9bf6-a1ac2a8f4680" 13194139534289 17592186045417 true] [17592186417741 1074 "If $b\\in \\text{Null}(A),$ then we must have $Ab=0.$ Substituting the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ab & =0 \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}2 & -6 \\\\ -1 & 3 \\\\ 4 & -12\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}k \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}2k-6 \\\\ -k+3 \\\\ 4k-12\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis corresponds to the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2k-6=0 \\\\ -k+3=0 \\\\ 4k-12=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand for each of these equations, we obtain $k=3.$" 13194139534289 17592186045417 true] [17592186417742 1068 #edb/ref 17592186417736 13194139534289 17592186045417 true] [17592186417742 1069 "q-111165" 13194139534289 17592186045417 true] [17592186417742 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139534289 17592186045417 true] [17592186417742 1071 "Consider the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -4\\end{aligned}].$ Find $\\text{Null}(A).$" 13194139534289 17592186045417 true] [17592186417742 1072 #uuid "f53050dc-6a1d-553b-afc7-7c5bd1dcb5bf" 13194139534289 17592186045417 true] [17592186417742 1074 "We need to solve the equation $Ax=0.$ First, we find the row echelon form of $A$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis corresponds to the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ {x}_{2}=0 \\\\ 0=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe second equation tells us that ${x}_{2}=0.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we get \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-3(0)=0\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=0.\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that $x=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$ is the only solution to this system.\n\nTherefore, $\\text{Null}(A)={0}.$" 13194139534289 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-065f9865-0513-58da-9b22-d96229767c84" 17592186417708 "answer-0b313932-8a2d-5efe-9590-f6798ae0a9bc" 17592186417709 "answer-1839cd87-9807-5099-aa1b-8c59eca72147" 17592186417710 "answer-267cb3d1-2ef0-50d2-827b-ba6571c4e7a7" 17592186417711 "answer-29619f9b-9f06-5558-89f7-4d0e65e0b6fe" 17592186417712 "answer-2bc79277-ae90-5b10-b515-d4f65951b373" 17592186417713 "answer-2ecdee28-7a39-54e8-b845-add658821807" 17592186417714 "answer-4200484a-68ef-5a68-826c-3f22c3f6744b" 17592186417715 "answer-43348635-a4e0-572f-b730-392f51070b83" 17592186417716 "answer-4345a24b-01f2-51a9-a9a3-ec26cb12faf8" 17592186417717 "answer-4c4607fe-b4f6-500f-b628-c9efb2f77b90" 17592186417718 "answer-59f64036-7331-5cd3-843e-78a74738a9d7" 17592186417719 "answer-63a9c9e9-789b-5e69-a3e9-b68cbdaf3c6e" 17592186417720 "answer-754f9b55-2a4f-56a1-a443-6730aeb9dbd2" 17592186417721 "answer-7d97603e-1f0e-5a8d-be4f-823054e6c132" 175